  "prefLabel": "Mec 301.04 “Primary dwelling” shall mean an existing single-family, stand-alone structure, owned, and occupied by a person or persons and such structure is used as the ind",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Mec 301.04 “Primary dwelling” shall mean an existing single-family, stand-alone structure, owned, and occupied by a person or persons and such structure is used as the individual's primary residence, and not a rental, income, vacation home, transient residence, hotel, or motel.\n\nSource. #10847, eff 7-1-15; ss by #13770, eff 12-10-23 (formerly Saf-Mec 301.24) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Mec 300)",
